    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive alignment, headlined by the dual-threat combination of **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). Both players anchor the top of their respective orders against favorable matchups, specifically benefiting from the \"Elite Speed\" priority; **Trea Turner** faces a soft landing against Lauer (5.41 xERA), and the high-upside matchup against Montero positions **Pete Crow-Armstrong** as a must-start for potential stolen base accumulation. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) also earns a premium spot today, as his platoon advantage against Lauer and his placement in the #2 hole elevate his profile despite a challenging park factor. **Yordan Alvarez** (75.00) remains a core cornerstone; his elite xwOBA of 0.480 maintains his daily efficiency score even against a relatively tougher arm in Alcantara.\n\nThe decision-making process for the fringes of the lineup was particularly tight today. While **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Junior Caminero** (66.77) secured their spots due to strong platoon indicators and high-value batting positions, the final UTIL slot went to **Carson Benge** (43.90). He narrowly edged out **Chase Meidroth** (42.55), who was relegated to the bench primarily due to a lower projected efficiency against a high-skill opponent in Alexander. While **Chase Meidroth** offers decent platoon upside, the optimizer favored **Carson Benge**'s projected volume in the heart of the order. Investors should monitor **Nelson Velazquez** (47.14) closely; while he remains in the lineup, his efficiency score is suppressed by Detmers' 3.56 xERA, making him a candidate for potential mid-game substitution if he fails to produce in his early at-bats. Meanwhile, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Lars Nootbaar** remain sidelined, leaving us to rely on our active roster to navigate today\u2019s pitching slate.",
